hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"373","'Umar ibn Hisham al-Qibti narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, from Abu Ja'far al-Razi, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, from Abu al-'Aliyah, he said: When booty was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would divide it into five fifths, then take a handful from the entire fifth and say: ""This is for the Ka'bah."" Then he would say: ""Do not assign a share to Allah, for to Allah belong the Hereafter and the first (life)."" Then he would take a share for himself, a share for the near relatives, a share for the orphans, a share for the poor, and a share for the wayfarer."
"374","Khushaysh ibn Asram narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Muhriz narrated to us: I asked al-Hasan about the anfal (spoils), he said: The spoils used to be gathered, and when gathered the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a share from them called the share of al-safi (the choicest part), which Allah assigned to him, then he narrated the hadith."
